diff --git a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-hid-lamparray b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-hid-lamparray
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..4d2b16614
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-hid-lamparray
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+What:		/sys/bus/hid/devices/<dev>/use_leds_uapi
+Date:		August 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.3
+Contact:	Cristian Mazzotta <cmmazzo@icloud.com>
+Description:
+		Controls whether the kernel drives the LampArray lamps
+		through the LED class interface or lets a userspace
+		application talk to the device.
+
+		Reading returns 1 if the kernel is driving the lamps, 0
+		otherwise.
+
+		Writing 1 restores the driver's cached RGB and brightness
+		values to every zone, discarding whatever userspace has
+		set. Writing 0 makes the driver stop touching the device;
+		writes to the per-zone LED class are accepted but ignored,
+		and the lamps are left untouched across system suspend and
+		resume. The LED class devices remain present in either mode.
+
+		Only 0 and 1 are accepted; any other value returns
+		-EINVAL.
